From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:45:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] board: mediatek-mobile: run chainloaded from LK as a
 boot-image kernel

Rework the mediatek-mobile board for the stock-LK handoff, modelled on
board/samsung/exynos-mobile and mach-snapdragon: LK loads U-Boot as the
kernel of an Android boot image and passes its own Android FDT in x0.

- Keep U-Boot's appended control DT (OF_SEPARATE with OF_BOARD) and parse
  LK's FDT before relocation for DRAM banks, /memreserve/ entries,
  reserved-memory regions with a reg property, the initrd window from
  /chosen and the MediaTek videolfb framebuffer tags.
- Relocate into the largest DRAM window below 4 GiB that avoids those
  reservations, LK's FDT, its initrd and the loaded image, instead of
  assuming a fixed 2 GiB bank. Build the MMU map from LK's banks with the
  no-map reservations left unmapped (the framebuffer stays mapped).
- Reserve LK's regions in LMB, allocate the load buffers below 4 GiB and
  take serial# from androidboot.serialno.
- Detect a FIT payload carried as the boot image's ramdisk: search the
  initrd window (LK may prepend other ramdisks), copy the FIT marked with
  "android-devices,payload" to an aligned buffer and export payload_addr.
- Forward LK's fixed reservations to the OS FDT in ft_board_setup() for
  both bootm and EFI.
- Point a simple-framebuffer node at LK's framebuffer from
  board_fix_fdt() only when LK reports one large enough.
- Define TARGET_MEDIATEK_MOBILE and its board name, add a generic
  mediatek_mobile_defconfig, and drop the TB373FU-specific environment and
  unsourced board Kconfig; devices provide their environment file.
- Remove the hard-coded TB373FU memory map and 2 GiB cap from mt6897.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
